From c9bc42a978e3d8aea8ffc992fc2323b87acc9503 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:24:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/43] usb_webcam: name UVC cameras after their product string

Every UVC camera got the same generic flavor name, so applications
showed two cameras as the same device. The name is now the product
string the device reports, for example "Integrated Camera" or
"HD Pro Webcam C920", without padding and cut to the media name
length without splitting a UTF-8 character. A device without a
product string keeps the generic name.

CamDeviceNameTest covers the trimming and cutting.

Signed-off-by: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: claude-opus-5-5
(cherry picked from commit 8f3c4fc4b94c00f26e3b392ca94d579b74f03ca8)
---
